# SukiSU manager installer: init -> shell transition.
#
# The oneshot service in ../../sukisu/init.sukisu_manager.rc runs
# `/system/bin/sh /system/etc/sukisu/install_manager.sh` with NO seclabel,
# so init must transition to the shell domain on exec. The stock rule
#   domain_trans(init, shell_exec, shell)
# from system/sepolicy/private/init.te does NOT take effect in this build:
# on a clean flash + reboot, init parses the .rc and fires
# `start sukisu_manager_install` at sys.boot_completed=1, then aborts with
# (dmesg):
#   Could not start service: File /system/bin/sh (labeled
#   "u:object_r:shell_exec:s0") has incorrect label or no domain transition
#   from u:r:init:s0 to another SELinux domain defined.
# (security_compute_create() found no type_transition for
# init + shell_exec -> *, so the service can never start and the manager
# is never installed; no flag file appears in /data/local/tmp/sukisu.)
#
# Re-apply the stock expansion here. Vendor policy is allowed to extend
# core domains, and no neverallow covers these rules (checked against
# system/sepolicy/{private,public}/*.te).
#
# NOTE: if a future base-policy update restores the stock rule, the build
# will fail loudly with a duplicate type_transition error. That failure
# means this file is obsolete: just delete it.
domain_trans(init, shell_exec, shell)
